IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rates-shared`

-- Land Tax Act 2004 (ACT), with the Taxation Administration (Amounts Payable--Land Tax) Determination 2026
-- (DI2026-152) and the Taxation Administration Act 1999 (ACT): land tax, quarter by quarter, on a residential parcel or
-- unit an individual owns, and the foreign ownership surcharge, for 2026-27.
--
-- Land tax is encoded here, in the Rates Act 2004's encoding folder, because its measure is the Rates Act s 13A average
-- unimproved value (Land Tax Act s 9(4): "AUV means the average unimproved value of the parcel of land under the Rates
-- Act 2004"), and the stable l4 cannot IMPORT across encoding folders. The Land Tax Act 2004 has no encoding folder of
-- its own (see NOTES.md).
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the owner", "a relevant person", "the
-- personal representative", "the commissioner". The owner's questions are in rates-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module
-- and restates no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED.
--   Land Tax Act 2004: s 7 (rent, tenancy agreement, tenant), s 8, s 8A (with (3) where an owner moves out), s 9,
--   s 10(1)(a)-(b), s 11A, s 11B, s 11C, s 11CA, s 11D (and (3), a regulative rule), s 11G, s 11H, s 11I, s 13 (its
--   decision as a fact), s 14 (a regulative rule), s 15, s 17 (a regulative rule), s 17A (foreign individual), s 17D,
--   s 17E, s 17F, s 18A and s 19 (in rates-shared.l4), s 19A, s 27(3), (4), (6), s 40. Rural land, and with it the
--   s 10(1)(d) exemption, answers `not covered`.
--   DI2026-152: s 4, s 5, s 6 and Table 1, s 7.
--   Taxation Administration Act 1999: div 5.2 (ss 30-35 and table 34, as applied by Land Tax Act s 19A(4)), s 67(2).
--
-- FIGURES. Every amount is read from DI2026-152, which commences on 1 July 2026: the quarters beginning 1 July 2026,
-- 1 October 2026, 1 January 2027 and 1 April 2027. Another quarter is `not covered`. The s 19 and s 19A interest rate
-- (TAA s 139) is not deposited: an input. The value of a penalty unit (Legislation Act 2001 s 133) is an input.
--
-- Edition: Land Tax Act 2004 A2004-4 R34 (effective 26 December 2025), and DI2026-152 as notified 30 June 2026, in
-- their own subject folders under subjects/au/act/; Taxation Administration Act 1999 A1999-4 R52 (effective 26 November
-- 2025).
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land Tax Act 2004 and the 2026 land tax determination -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `s 9 and DI2026-152 s 6 -- the yearly figures`

-- s 9(1): "Land tax at the appropriate rate is imposed for a quarter on each parcel of rateable land that is residential
-- land." (3)(b): "FC+(AUV×P)". (4): "AUV means the average unimproved value of the parcel of land under the Rates Act
-- 2004. FC means the fixed charge determined under the Taxation Administration Act, section 139 for the parcel of land.
-- P means the percentage rate determined under the Taxation Administration Act, section 139 for the parcel of land."
-- DI2026-152 s 6: "(a) FC (or fixed charge) is $1,778; and (b) P (or percentage rate) is the amount listed in column 2
-- of Table 1 opposite the base value listed in column 1." s 3: "base value, of a parcel of land, means -- (a) the AUV of
-- the parcel; or (b) for a unit -- the AUVRU worked out for the unit."
`the land tax fixed charge (DI2026-152 s 6(a))` MEANS 1778

-- DI2026-152 Table 1 Percentage rates--land tax:
--   <= $150 000                     0.54% of the base value
--   > $150 000, <= $275 000         $810 plus 0.64% of the part of the base value that is more than $150 000
--   > $275 000, <= $1 000 000       $1,610 plus 1.24% ... more than $275 000
--   > $1 000 000, <= $2 000 000     $10,600 plus 1.25% ... more than $1 000 000
--   > $2 000 000                    $23,100 plus 1.26% ... more than $2 000 000
`DI2026-152 Table 1` MEANS
    LIST `Table row` WITH `above` IS 2000000, `base` IS 23100, `rate` IS 1.26%
         `Table row` WITH `above` IS 1000000, `base` IS 10600, `rate` IS 1.25%
         `Table row` WITH `above` IS 275000,  `base` IS 1610,  `rate` IS 1.24%
         `Table row` WITH `above` IS 150000,  `base` IS 810,   `rate` IS 0.64%
         `Table row` WITH `above` IS 0,       `base` IS 0,     `rate` IS 0.54%

-- DI2026-152 s 7: "For the purposes of section 17E (4) of the Act, I determine that P (or percentage rate) is 0.75% of
-- the base value."
`the foreign ownership surcharge rate (DI2026-152 s 7)` MEANS 0.75%

§§ `DI2026-152 s 4 -- the amount for a quarter`

-- s 4(1): "a determined amount payable for a quarter is worked out as follows: determined amount × (days in
-- quarter)/(days in year)". The example: "FC of $1 778 ... The quarter beginning 1 October 2026 has 92 days. The
-- relevant financial year has 365 days. The determined FC for the quarter is $1 778 × (92)/(365) = $448.15." (2):
-- "determined amount includes -- (a) FC (or fixed charge) and P (or percentage rate) determined under section 6 ... and
-- (b) P (or percentage rate) determined under section 7". READING: each determined amount is scaled to the quarter and
-- rounded to the cent (Land Tax Act s 40(1)) before they are added, as the example rounds the FC (NOTES.md finding 16).
GIVEN `the yearly amount` IS A NUMBER, `the quarter start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount for the quarter under DI2026-152 s 4 of` `the yearly amount` `starting` `the quarter start` MEANS
    `to the nearest cent` ((`the yearly amount` TIMES (`the days in the quarter starting` `the quarter start`)) DIVIDED BY `the days in the year 2026-27`)

§§ `ss 7, 8 and 8A -- rented, and payable on the 1st day of a quarter`

-- s 7: "tenancy agreement -- (a) means an agreement under which a person gives someone else, for value, a right of
-- occupation of a parcel of land for use as a residence ... but (b) does not include an agreement giving a right of
-- occupation only as a boarder or lodger." s 8(1): "a parcel of land or dwelling is not taken to be rented only because a
-- tenant is liable to pay for rates, repairs, maintenance or insurance". (2): "a parcel of land or dwelling is taken to
-- be rented if it is rented on the 1st day of a quarter." s 8A(1): "land tax is payable on a parcel of land for a
-- quarter if it is payable on the 1st day of the quarter." (2): "... if it is not exempt under this part from land tax
-- on that day." (3): "If an exemption under this part stops applying to a parcel of land, land tax is payable on the 1st
-- day of the quarter after the date the exemption stops applying."
-- Who occupies the parcel on the 1st day of the quarter, and on what terms. A boarder or lodger is not a tenant (s 7);
-- an occupant who pays only the rates, repairs, maintenance and insurance is not a tenant either (s 8(1)), and is the
-- s 11H occupant.
DECLARE `Occupancy on the 1st day of the quarter` IS ONE OF
    `an owner occupies it as their principal place of residence`
    `a person with a life or term interest in it under a will occupies it as their principal place of residence`
    `a person occupies it who pays no rent, or no more than the rates, repairs, maintenance and insurance`
    `it is rented to a tenant`
    `no one occupies it`

-- The earlier events from which an exemption runs on into a later quarter (ss 11B, 11C, 11CA, 11D).
DECLARE `Earlier event` IS ONE OF
    `none of these`
    `an owner stopped occupying it as their principal place of residence (s 11B)`
    `the owner became the owner, to occupy it as their principal place of residence (s 11C)`
    `it stopped being rented so the owner could occupy it as their principal place of residence (s 11CA)`
    `the owner who occupied it as their principal place of residence died (s 11D)`

-- Every fact the position for one quarter turns on, for one parcel or unit.
DECLARE `Land tax quarter` HAS
    `the first day of the quarter`                                           IS A DATE
    `kind`                                                                   IS A `Kind of land`
    `an owner is a corporation or a trustee`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `occupancy`                                                              IS AN `Occupancy on the 1st day of the quarter`
    `the event`                                                              IS AN `Earlier event`
    `the date of the event`                                                  IS A DATE
    `within 3 months after the event the owner occupied it as their principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within 3 months after the event it was rented to a tenant, other than the seller for up to 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `since the death it has been registered only in the name of the deceased owner or the personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner has extended the 2-year period after the death to cover the quarter (s 11E)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner and their domestic partner own more than 1 parcel and the s 11A exemption is taken for another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner is satisfied the owner and their partner have separated, with no reasonable likelihood of resuming cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner is satisfied the parcel became unfit for occupation as a place of residence (s 11I)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a certificate of occupancy was issued for it, on`                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the commissioner is satisfied it is fit for occupation again`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner has exempted it on compassionate grounds for a period including the quarter (s 13)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has more than 1 dwelling, one occupied as in s 15(1)(b) and another rented to a tenant` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Land tax exemption` IS ONE OF
    `s 11A: an owner's principal place of residence`
    `s 11B: the 1st quarter after an owner moved out (and it is not rented)`
    `s 11C: the 1st quarter after becoming the owner, to move in`
    `s 11CA: the 1st quarter after a rental ended, to move in`
    `s 11D: 2 years after the death of the owner who lived there (or as extended)`
    `s 11G: a life tenant's principal place of residence`
    `s 11H: occupied rent-free, or for no more than the outgoings`
    `s 11I: unfit for occupation as a place of residence`
    `s 13: a compassionate exemption`

DECLARE `Land tax position` IS ONE OF
    `land tax is payable for the quarter (s 9)`
    `land tax is payable on the rented dwelling's share (s 15)`
    `exempt` HAS `under` IS A `Land tax exemption`
    `not payable for the quarter: the owner's home exemption stopped on or after its 1st day, and land tax is payable only from the 1st day of the next quarter (s 8A(3))`

GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not covered`
`the gap for the quarter` `q` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`q`'s `the first day of the quarter` `is the first day of a quarter of 2026-27`)
        THEN JUST `the day is outside the year 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027: only the 2026 determinations are deposited`
        IF `q`'s `an owner is a corporation or a trustee`
        THEN JUST `land owned, wholly or partly, by a corporation or a trustee (Rates Act s 20A(2), Land Tax Act ss 16 and 27(5)) is not encoded`
        OTHERWISE `the gap for the kind of land` (`q`'s `kind`)

GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is rented on the 1st day of` `q` IF
    `q`'s `occupancy` EQUALS `it is rented to a tenant`

GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the quarter is the 1st quarter after the event in` `q` IF
    (`q`'s `the first day of the quarter`) `is the same day as` (`the first day of the quarter after` (`q`'s `the date of the event`))

-- s 11A(1): "This section applies if a parcel of land is, on the 1st day of a quarter -- (a) owned by someone other than
-- a corporation or trustee; and (b) occupied as the principal place of residence of 1 or more owners of the parcel of
-- land. (2) The parcel of land is exempt from land tax. (3) However, for 2 people in a domestic partnership with more
-- than 1 parcel of land, only 1 parcel may be eligible for an exemption under this section unless the commissioner is
-- satisfied the people have separated and there is no reasonable likelihood of cohabitation being resumed."
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11A exempts` `q` IF
        `q`'s `occupancy` EQUALS `an owner occupies it as their principal place of residence`
    AND (    NOT (`q`'s `the owner and their domestic partner own more than 1 parcel and the s 11A exemption is taken for another`)
         OR  `q`'s `the commissioner is satisfied the owner and their partner have separated, with no reasonable likelihood of resuming cohabitation`)

-- s 11B(1): "This section applies if an owner of a parcel of land ... (a) occupies the parcel as the principal place of
-- residence; and (b) stops occupying the parcel as the principal place of residence. (2) The parcel of land is exempt
-- from land tax for the 1st quarter after the date the owner stops occupying the parcel as the principal place of
-- residence. ... (3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the parcel of land is rented by a tenant." READING: "rented" as on
-- the 1st day of that quarter (s 8(2)).
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11B exempts` `q` IF
        `q`'s `the event` EQUALS `an owner stopped occupying it as their principal place of residence (s 11B)`
    AND `the quarter is the 1st quarter after the event in` `q`
    AND NOT (`it is rented on the 1st day of` `q`)

-- s 11C(1): "This section applies if a person, other than a corporation or trustee, becomes the owner (the new owner) of
-- a parcel of land, to be occupied by the new owner as their principal place of residence. (2) The parcel of land is
-- exempt from land tax for the 1st quarter after the date the new owner becomes the owner of the parcel. ... (3)
-- Subsection (2) does not apply if, within 3 months after the date the new owner becomes the owner of the parcel -- (a)
-- the new owner does not occupy the parcel as their principal place of residence; or (b) the parcel is rented by a
-- tenant, other than the seller of the parcel under an agreement with the new owner for a period of not longer than 3
-- months."
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11C exempts` `q` IF
        `q`'s `the event` EQUALS `the owner became the owner, to occupy it as their principal place of residence (s 11C)`
    AND `the quarter is the 1st quarter after the event in` `q`
    AND `q`'s `within 3 months after the event the owner occupied it as their principal place of residence`
    AND NOT (`q`'s `within 3 months after the event it was rented to a tenant, other than the seller for up to 3 months`)

-- s 11CA(1): "This section applies if a parcel of land ... stops being rented so it can be occupied by the owner of the
-- parcel as their principal place of residence. (2) The parcel of land is exempt from land tax for the 1st quarter after
-- the date the parcel stopped being rented. ... (3) Subsection (2) does not apply if, within 3 months after the date the
-- parcel stopped being rented -- (a) the owner does not occupy the parcel as their principal place of residence; or (b)
-- the parcel is rented by a tenant."
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11CA exempts` `q` IF
        `q`'s `the event` EQUALS `it stopped being rented so the owner could occupy it as their principal place of residence (s 11CA)`
    AND `the quarter is the 1st quarter after the event in` `q`
    AND `q`'s `within 3 months after the event the owner occupied it as their principal place of residence`
    AND NOT (`q`'s `within 3 months after the event it was rented to a tenant, other than the seller for up to 3 months`)

-- s 11D(1): "This section applies if -- (a) a parcel of land, other than a parcel of land owned by a corporation or
-- trustee, is occupied as the principal place of residence by the owner of the parcel; and (b) the owner dies. (2) The
-- parcel of land is exempt from land tax for 2 years after the date of the owner's death if, during the 2-year period,
-- the parcel is registered in the name of -- (a) the deceased owner; or (b) the personal representative." s 11E(1): the
-- commissioner "may extend the period" (a FACT).
-- READING: "2 years after the date of the owner's death" runs from the day after the death and ends at the end of its
-- second anniversary: for a death on 15 March 2025, the last day is 15 March 2027. The same day ends the period for an
-- application under s 11D(3) (below), so the two rules cannot disagree. A quarter is within the 2 years if its 1st day
-- (s 8A(1)-(2)) is on or before the last day (NOTES.md finding 27).
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the 2-year period after a death on` `the day of the death` MEANS
    `the date` 24 `months after` `the day of the death`

GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11D exempts` `q` IF
        `q`'s `the event` EQUALS `the owner who occupied it as their principal place of residence died (s 11D)`
    AND `q`'s `since the death it has been registered only in the name of the deceased owner or the personal representative`
    AND (    (`q`'s `the first day of the quarter`) `is on or before` (`the last day of the 2-year period after a death on` (`q`'s `the date of the event`))
         OR  `q`'s `the commissioner has extended the 2-year period after the death to cover the quarter (s 11E)`)

-- s 11G(1): "This section applies if a parcel of land is, on the 1st day of a quarter -- (a) owned by someone other than
-- a corporation or trustee; and (b) occupied as the principal place of residence of a person having a life or term
-- interest in the parcel of land under a will. (2) The parcel of land is exempt from land tax. (3) Subsection (2) does
-- not apply if the parcel of land is rented to the person or another person."
-- s 11H(1): "This section applies if a parcel of land is, on the 1st day of a quarter -- (a) owned by someone other than
-- a corporation or trustee; and (b) occupied by a person who -- (i) is liable only to pay an amount that is not more
-- than the total amount required for rates, repairs, maintenance and insurance in relation to the parcel; or (ii) pays
-- no rent for the parcel. (2) The parcel of land is exempt from land tax."
-- s 11I(1): "This section applies if the commissioner is satisfied that a parcel of land is, or has become, unfit for
-- occupation as a place of residence." (2): "exempt from land tax after the date the parcel became unfit ..., until --
-- (a) the end of the quarter following the quarter in which a certificate of occupancy is issued for the parcel; or (b)
-- the commissioner is satisfied that the parcel is fit for occupation as a place of residence. (3) Subsection (2) does
-- not apply if the parcel of land is rented by a tenant."
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11I exempts` `q` IF
        `q`'s `the commissioner is satisfied the parcel became unfit for occupation as a place of residence (s 11I)`
    AND NOT (`q`'s `the commissioner is satisfied it is fit for occupation again`)
    AND NOT (`it is rented on the 1st day of` `q`)
    AND `the certificate period has not ended`
    WHERE
        `the certificate period has not ended` MEANS
            CONSIDER `q`'s `a certificate of occupancy was issued for it, on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST `the day issued` THEN
                (`q`'s `the first day of the quarter`) `is on or before` (`the first day of the quarter after` `the day issued`)

-- s 8A(3): "If an exemption under this part stops applying to a parcel of land, land tax is payable on the 1st day of
-- the quarter after the date the exemption stops applying." Where an owner stops occupying the parcel as their principal
-- place of residence (s 11B(1)), the s 11A exemption stops applying on that date. So land tax is not payable for a
-- quarter whose 1st day is before the 1st day of the quarter after that date, even if no one occupies the parcel on
-- the quarter's 1st day. READING: a quarter beginning on the date itself is not "after" it, as for s 11B (NOTES.md
-- findings 20 and 26). s 17D(3) says the same of the foreign ownership surcharge.
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8A(3) puts land tax off past` `q` IF
        `q`'s `the event` EQUALS `an owner stopped occupying it as their principal place of residence (s 11B)`
    AND DATE_SERIAL (`q`'s `the first day of the quarter`) LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the first day of the quarter after` (`q`'s `the date of the event`))

-- s 15(1): "This section applies if -- (a) a parcel of residential land owned by someone other than a corporation or
-- trustee contains multiple dwellings; and (b) at least 1 of the dwellings is occupied -- (i) as the principal place of
-- residence of 1 or more owners ...; or (ii) as the principal place of residence of a person having a life or term
-- interest in the parcel of land under a will; or (iii) by a person who pays no rent ...; and (c) at least 1 of the
-- dwellings is rented by a tenant. (2) Section 10 ... and section 11 ... do not apply to the parcel of land."
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15 applies to` `q` IF
    `q`'s `it has more than 1 dwelling, one occupied as in s 15(1)(b) and another rented to a tenant`

-- s 9(2): "land tax is not imposed on a parcel of land that is exempt under section 10 or section 11." s 10(1)(a) lists
-- the exemptions of ss 11A-11I; (b) "a parcel of residential land owned by an individual if the parcel is exempted under
-- section 13 (Decision on compassionate application)" (the decision is a FACT).
-- The position on the facts, for any quarter: no figure is needed, so the year is not checked here.
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH A `Land tax position`
`the land tax position on the facts of` `q` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 15 applies to` `q` THEN `land tax is payable on the rented dwelling's share (s 15)`
        IF `s 11A exempts` `q` THEN `exempt` `s 11A: an owner's principal place of residence`
        IF `q`'s `occupancy` EQUALS `a person with a life or term interest in it under a will occupies it as their principal place of residence`
        THEN `exempt` `s 11G: a life tenant's principal place of residence`
        IF `q`'s `occupancy` EQUALS `a person occupies it who pays no rent, or no more than the rates, repairs, maintenance and insurance`
        THEN `exempt` `s 11H: occupied rent-free, or for no more than the outgoings`
        IF `s 8A(3) puts land tax off past` `q`
        THEN `not payable for the quarter: the owner's home exemption stopped on or after its 1st day, and land tax is payable only from the 1st day of the next quarter (s 8A(3))`
        IF `s 11B exempts` `q` THEN `exempt` `s 11B: the 1st quarter after an owner moved out (and it is not rented)`
        IF `s 11C exempts` `q` THEN `exempt` `s 11C: the 1st quarter after becoming the owner, to move in`
        IF `s 11CA exempts` `q` THEN `exempt` `s 11CA: the 1st quarter after a rental ended, to move in`
        IF `s 11D exempts` `q` THEN `exempt` `s 11D: 2 years after the death of the owner who lived there (or as extended)`
        IF `s 11I exempts` `q` THEN `exempt` `s 11I: unfit for occupation as a place of residence`
        IF `q`'s `the commissioner has exempted it on compassionate grounds for a period including the quarter (s 13)`
        THEN `exempt` `s 13: a compassionate exemption`
        OTHERWISE `land tax is payable for the quarter (s 9)`

GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Land tax position`
`the land tax position for` `q` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the gap for the quarter` `q`
    WHEN JUST `gap` THEN `not covered` `gap`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `answered` (`the land tax position on the facts of` `q`)

GIVEN `the position` IS A `Land tax position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `land tax is payable in` `the position` IF
    CONSIDER `the position`
    WHEN `land tax is payable for the quarter (s 9)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `land tax is payable on the rented dwelling's share (s 15)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 9, 15 and 27 -- the land tax for a quarter`

-- What the amount turns on. The floor areas are read only under s 15 or s 27(4); the unit entitlements only for a unit.
-- s 15(5): "FA means the floor area of the rented dwelling. ... TFA means the total floor area of all dwellings on the
-- parcel of land." s 27(7): "FA means the floor area of the dwelling that is rented. ... TFA means the total floor area
-- of the unit."
DECLARE `Land tax parcel` HAS
    `the unimproved values as at 1 January, most recent first` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `the unit entitlements`                                    IS A `Unit entitlements`
    `FA`                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `TFA`                                                      IS A NUMBER

-- The amount questions need the AUV (s 9(4), s 17E(4)). A parcel with no unimproved value given has none, and the
-- amount is `not covered`; the AUV below is read only after this check.
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`, `p` IS A `Land tax parcel`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not covered`
`the gap for the quarter and parcel` `q` `p` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the gap for the quarter` `q`
    WHEN JUST `gap` THEN JUST `gap`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the average unimproved value under s 13A of` (`p`'s `the unimproved values as at 1 January, most recent first`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `no unimproved value of the parcel was given (the valuation, Rates Act pt 2, is out of scope)`
        WHEN JUST `auv` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `p` IS A `Land tax parcel`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the parcel AUV of` `p` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the average unimproved value under s 13A of` (`p`'s `the unimproved values as at 1 January, most recent first`)
    WHEN JUST `auv` THEN `auv`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- The yearly fixed part and variable part, before DI2026-152 s 4 scales them to the quarter.
-- s 9(3)(b): FC + (AUV × P), P the Table 1 amount on the AUV.
-- s 15(3): "the AUV of the parcel of land is the amount worked out as follows: AUV × (FA)/(TFA)"; (4): "the FC for the
-- parcel of land is ... FC × (FA)/(TFA)". Land Tax Act s 40(2): "in working out the average unimproved value under
-- section 15 (3) ... or section 27 (4), (5) or (6) ..., any fraction of a dollar in the amount worked out must be
-- disregarded."
-- s 27(6): "FC + (AUVRUP × (UE)/(TUER))", AUVRUP = AUVRU × P, P the Table 1 amount on the base value AUVRU.
-- s 27(4): "(FC × (FA)/(TFA)) + (AUVRUP × (UE)/(TUER) × (FA)/(TFA))" for a unit with multiple dwellings, one occupied
-- as in s 27(4)(c) and one rented.
DECLARE `Yearly land tax parts` HAS
    `fixed part`    IS A NUMBER
    `variable part` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `is a unit` IS A BOOLEAN, `under s 15` IS A BOOLEAN, `p` IS A `Land tax parcel`
GIVETH A `Yearly land tax parts`
`the yearly land tax parts for` `is a unit` `with s 15` `under s 15` `on` `p` MEANS
    IF `is a unit`
    THEN `Yearly land tax parts` WITH
             `fixed part`    IS `the land tax fixed charge (DI2026-152 s 6(a))` TIMES `the floor share`
             `variable part` IS ((`the column 2 amount in` `DI2026-152 Table 1` `for` (`AUVRU for` `AUV` `and` (`p`'s `the unit entitlements`))) TIMES ((`p`'s `the unit entitlements`'s `UE`) DIVIDED BY (`p`'s `the unit entitlements`'s `TUER`))) TIMES `the floor share`
    ELSE `Yearly land tax parts` WITH
             `fixed part`    IS `the land tax fixed charge (DI2026-152 s 6(a))` TIMES `the floor share`
             `variable part` IS `the column 2 amount in` `DI2026-152 Table 1` `for` (IF `under s 15` THEN `with any fraction of a dollar disregarded` (`AUV` TIMES `the floor share`) ELSE `AUV`)
    WHERE
        `AUV` MEANS `the parcel AUV of` `p`
        `the floor share` MEANS
            IF `under s 15` AND `p`'s `TFA` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN (`p`'s `FA`) DIVIDED BY (`p`'s `TFA`)
            ELSE 1

-- The land tax for the quarter: nil if exempt; otherwise each part scaled by DI2026-152 s 4 and added.
GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`, `p` IS A `Land tax parcel`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the land tax for the quarter of` `q` `on` `p` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the gap for the quarter and parcel` `q` `p`
    WHEN JUST `gap` THEN `not covered` `gap`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF NOT (`land tax is payable in` `the position`)
        THEN `answered` 0
        ELSE `answered` ((`the amount for the quarter under DI2026-152 s 4 of` (`the parts`'s `fixed part`) `starting` (`q`'s `the first day of the quarter`))
                        PLUS (`the amount for the quarter under DI2026-152 s 4 of` (`the parts`'s `variable part`) `starting` (`q`'s `the first day of the quarter`)))
    WHERE
        `the position` MEANS `the land tax position on the facts of` `q`
        `the parts` MEANS `the yearly land tax parts for` (`q`'s `kind` EQUALS `a residential unit in a units plan`) `with s 15` (`the position` EQUALS `land tax is payable on the rented dwelling's share (s 15)`) `on` `p`

-- The first quarter for which land tax is payable after an owner moves out of their home and leaves it rented or empty
-- (ss 8A(3), 11B), taken from the position for each quarter in turn, so that this answer and `the land tax position
-- for` cannot disagree. The quarter containing the day (or beginning on it) is put off by s 8A(3); the 1st quarter after
-- is exempt under s 11B unless it is rented on its 1st day; the quarter after that is reached by neither, and an empty or
-- rented home has no other exemption (s 9(1); NOTES.md finding 14). The facts for ss 11C-15 are held at "no"; the kind of
-- land is not read by the position.
GIVEN `the quarter start` IS A DATE, `the day the owner moved out` IS A DATE, `who occupies it` IS AN `Occupancy on the 1st day of the quarter`
GIVETH A `Land tax quarter`
`the facts for the quarter starting` `the quarter start` `for a move out on` `the day the owner moved out` `with` `who occupies it` MEANS
    `Land tax quarter` WITH
        `the first day of the quarter`                                           IS `the quarter start`
        `kind`                                                                   IS `residential land that is not a unit`
        `an owner is a corporation or a trustee`                                 IS FALSE
        `occupancy`                                                              IS `who occupies it`
        `the event`                                                              IS `an owner stopped occupying it as their principal place of residence (s 11B)`
        `the date of the event`                                                  IS `the day the owner moved out`
        `within 3 months after the event the owner occupied it as their principal place of residence` IS FALSE
        `within 3 months after the event it was rented to a tenant, other than the seller for up to 3 months` IS FALSE
        `since the death it has been registered only in the name of the deceased owner or the personal representative` IS FALSE
        `the commissioner has extended the 2-year period after the death to cover the quarter (s 11E)` IS FALSE
        `the owner and their domestic partner own more than 1 parcel and the s 11A exemption is taken for another` IS FALSE
        `the commissioner is satisfied the owner and their partner have separated, with no reasonable likelihood of resuming cohabitation` IS FALSE
        `the commissioner is satisfied the parcel became unfit for occupation as a place of residence (s 11I)` IS FALSE
        `a certificate of occupancy was issued for it, on`                       IS NOTHING
        `the commissioner is satisfied it is fit for occupation again`           IS FALSE
        `the commissioner has exempted it on compassionate grounds for a period including the quarter (s 13)` IS FALSE
        `it has more than 1 dwelling, one occupied as in s 15(1)(b) and another rented to a tenant` IS FALSE

GIVEN `the quarter start` IS A DATE, `the day the owner moved out` IS A DATE, `who occupies it` IS AN `Occupancy on the 1st day of the quarter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `land tax is payable for the quarter starting` `the quarter start` `after a move out on` `the day the owner moved out` `with` `who occupies it` IF
    `land tax is payable in` (`the land tax position on the facts of` (`the facts for the quarter starting` `the quarter start` `for a move out on` `the day the owner moved out` `with` `who occupies it`))

GIVEN `the day the owner moved out` IS A DATE, `rented on the 1st day of the next quarter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the first quarter of land tax after moving out on` `the day the owner moved out` `when rented at the next quarter` `rented on the 1st day of the next quarter` MEANS
    IF `land tax is payable for the quarter starting` `the quarter containing the day` `after a move out on` `the day the owner moved out` `with` `no one occupies it`
    THEN `the quarter containing the day`
    ELSE IF `land tax is payable for the quarter starting` `the next quarter` `after a move out on` `the day the owner moved out` `with` `the occupancy at the next quarter`
         THEN `the next quarter`
         ELSE `the date` 3 `months after` `the next quarter`
    WHERE
        `the quarter containing the day` MEANS `the first day of the quarter containing` `the day the owner moved out`
        `the next quarter` MEANS `the first day of the quarter after` `the day the owner moved out`
        `the occupancy at the next quarter` MEANS
            IF `rented on the 1st day of the next quarter` THEN `it is rented to a tenant` ELSE `no one occupies it`

§§ `Part 2A -- the foreign ownership surcharge`

-- s 17A: "foreign individual means an individual who, on the 1st day of a quarter, is not -- (a) an Australian citizen;
-- or (b) a permanent resident; or (c) ordinarily resident in Australia or an external territory." "foreign person -- (a)
-- means -- (i) a foreign individual; ... but (b) does not include a personal representative of a deceased person."
-- "permanent resident means -- (a) a person who holds a permanent visa under the Migration Act 1958 (Cwlth), section 30
-- (1); or (b) a New Zealand citizen who holds a special category visa under the Migration Act 1958 (Cwlth), section 32."
-- The three statuses are FACTS (borrowed terms). READING: "is not (a) ...; or (b) ...; or (c) ..." means none of them,
-- so a person ordinarily resident in Australia is not a foreign individual whatever their visa (NOTES.md finding 19).
-- Foreign corporations and trusts (ss 17B, 17C) are outside the seat.
DECLARE `Residence facts` HAS
    `an Australian citizen`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a permanent resident (a permanent visa, or a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordinarily resident in Australia or an external territory`                    IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `r` IS A `Residence facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a foreign individual under s 17A` `r` IF
        NOT (`r`'s `an Australian citizen`)
    AND NOT (`r`'s `a permanent resident (a permanent visa, or a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa)`)
    AND NOT (`r`'s `ordinarily resident in Australia or an external territory`)

-- s 17E(1): the surcharge "is imposed for a quarter on each parcel of rateable land that is -- (a) residential land;
-- and (b) on the 1st day of the quarter, owned by a foreign person." (2): "However, a foreign ownership surcharge is not
-- imposed on a parcel of land that is exempt under -- (a) section 10 ..., other than section 10 (1) (a) (vii); or (b)
-- section 11". s 10(1)(a)(vii) is s 11H (nil or nominal rent). (3): "(a) for a unit that is part of a unit subdivision
-- -- ... AUVRUP× (UE)/(TUER); or (b) in any other case -- ... AUV×P". s 17F(2): where the parcel is owned by foreign and
-- other people, the amount is multiplied by "(FI)/(AI)", "FI means the value of all interests in the parcel or unit held
-- by foreign people", "AI means the value of all interests in the parcel of land."
-- INFERENCE: where s 15 applies, s 15(2) disapplies ss 10 and 11 to the parcel, so the surcharge falls on the whole AUV
-- (s 15 changes only the land tax AUV and FC).
-- s 17D(3), in the words of s 8A(3): "If an exemption under this part stops applying to a parcel of land, a foreign
-- ownership surcharge is payable on the 1st day of the quarter after the date the exemption stops applying." The s 11A
-- exemption is one under pt 2A too (s 17E(2)(b)), so the quarter s 8A(3) puts off is put off for the surcharge as well.
GIVEN `the position` IS A `Land tax position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surcharge is imposed in` `the position` IF
    CONSIDER `the position`
    WHEN `exempt` `e` THEN `e` EQUALS `s 11H: occupied rent-free, or for no more than the outgoings`
    WHEN `land tax is payable for the quarter (s 9)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `land tax is payable on the rented dwelling's share (s 15)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `q` IS A `Land tax quarter`, `p` IS A `Land tax parcel`, `the foreign share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the foreign ownership surcharge for the quarter of` `q` `on` `p` `with a foreign share of` `the foreign share` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the gap for the quarter and parcel` `q` `p`
    WHEN JUST `gap` THEN `not covered` `gap`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF NOT (`the surcharge is imposed in` (`the land tax position on the facts of` `q`)) OR `the foreign share` AT MOST 0
        THEN `answered` 0
        ELSE `answered` (`the amount for the quarter under DI2026-152 s 4 of` (`the yearly surcharge` TIMES `the foreign share`) `starting` (`q`'s `the first day of the quarter`))
    WHERE
        `AUV` MEANS `the parcel AUV of` `p`
        `the yearly surcharge` MEANS
            IF `q`'s `kind` EQUALS `a residential unit in a units plan`
            THEN ((`AUVRU for` `AUV` `and` (`p`'s `the unit entitlements`)) TIMES `the foreign ownership surcharge rate (DI2026-152 s 7)`) TIMES ((`p`'s `the unit entitlements`'s `UE`) DIVIDED BY (`p`'s `the unit entitlements`'s `TUER`))
            ELSE `AUV` TIMES `the foreign ownership surcharge rate (DI2026-152 s 7)`

§§ `s 14 -- the commissioner must be told of a change`

-- s 14(1): "This section applies in relation to a parcel of land that is leased for residential purposes if -- (a) land
-- tax or a foreign ownership surcharge is not imposed on the parcel; or (b) the parcel is exempt from land tax or a
-- foreign ownership surcharge. (2) A relevant person for the parcel of land must tell the commissioner -- (a) of any
-- change in circumstances in relation to the parcel that would cause land tax or a foreign ownership surcharge to
-- become payable for the parcel; and (b) the date of the change in circumstances." (3): "... not later than 30 days
-- after the date the circumstances change." (4): "relevant person ... means -- (a) the owner of the parcel of land; or
-- (b) if the owner has authorised an agent to act on the owner's behalf in relation to the parcel -- the agent; or (c)
-- if the owner has died -- the personal representative." s 14 states no penalty. Note 1: "It is an offence to fail to
-- notify the commissioner under this section (see Taxation Administration Act, s 67 (2))" -- TAA s 67(2): "Maximum
-- penalty: 50 penalty units." s 19A: if "the owner of the parcel of land fails to comply with section 14", interest runs
-- "from the end of 30 days after the 1st day of the 1st quarter for which the tax is imposed" and TAA div 5.2 (penalty
-- tax) applies "as if -- (a) the owner's failure to comply with section 14 were a tax default". Clock: days from the date
-- of the change.
`the days to tell the commissioner (s 14(3))` MEANS 30
`the maximum penalty under TAA s 67(2), in penalty units` MEANS 50

GIVEN `the relevant person` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
DECIDE `s 14 -- a relevant person must tell the commissioner within 30 days of a change that makes land tax payable` IS
    PARTY `the relevant person`
    MUST  `tell the commissioner of the change in circumstances and its date`
    WITHIN `the days to tell the commissioner (s 14(3))`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the relevant person` BECAUSE "Land Tax Act s 14(2)-(3): the commissioner was not told of the change within 30 days; TAA s 67(2): maximum penalty 50 penalty units; s 19A: the owner pays interest from 30 days after the 1st day of the 1st quarter of the tax, and penalty tax under TAA div 5.2"

-- s 19A(2): "The owner is liable to pay interest on the amount of land tax from the end of 30 days after the 1st day of
-- the 1st quarter for which the tax is imposed." (3): interest "for each month that the amount is payable; and (b) on
-- the 1st day of that month; and (c) at the interest rate applying to that day; and (d) on the total amount of land tax
-- that is payable". FINDING: s 19A has no counterpart of s 19(2) (a part of a month counts as a whole month). READING:
-- the months are counted as under s 19 (NOTES.md finding 21).
GIVEN `the 1st day of the 1st quarter of the tax` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day s 19A interest runs to the end of, for a quarter starting` `the 1st day of the 1st quarter of the tax` MEANS
    `the day that is` 30 `days after` `the 1st day of the 1st quarter of the tax`

-- TAA div 5.2 as s 19A(4) applies it: "a reference to the amount of tax unpaid were a reference to the amount of land
-- tax payable". s 31(1): "25% of the amount of tax unpaid"; (2) up to 50% (delay, incorrect information, a second
-- default); (4) up to 75% (intentional disregard); (5) none if the commissioner is satisfied of reasonable care or
-- circumstances beyond the taxpayer's control. s 32: "reduced by 80% if, before the commissioner informs the taxpayer
-- that an investigation ... is to be carried out, the taxpayer discloses"; s 33: "reduced by 20%" if disclosed after
-- being told and before it is begun; s 34: 90% for concealment; s 35: "No penalty tax is payable if the amount that
-- would otherwise be payable is less than $20." What the commissioner is satisfied of is a FACT.
DECLARE `What the commissioner is satisfied of` IS ONE OF
    `reasonable care, or circumstances beyond the owner's control (TAA s 31(5))`
    `nothing more than the default (TAA s 31(1))`
    `delay, incorrect or incomplete information, or a second default (TAA s 31(2))`
    `intentional disregard of a tax law (TAA s 31(4))`
    `concealment after being told of an investigation (TAA s 34)`

DECLARE `Disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `no disclosure`
    `disclosure in writing before being told of an investigation (TAA s 32)`
    `disclosure in writing after being told of an investigation, before it began (TAA s 33)`

GIVEN `the finding` IS A `What the commissioner is satisfied of`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic penalty tax percentage for` `the finding` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the finding`
    WHEN `reasonable care, or circumstances beyond the owner's control (TAA s 31(5))` THEN 0
    WHEN `nothing more than the default (TAA s 31(1))` THEN 25
    WHEN `delay, incorrect or incomplete information, or a second default (TAA s 31(2))` THEN 50
    WHEN `intentional disregard of a tax law (TAA s 31(4))` THEN 75
    WHEN `concealment after being told of an investigation (TAA s 34)` THEN 90

-- Table 34: basic 0/25/50/75/90; voluntary disclosure 0/5/10/15/90; disclosure before investigation 0/20/40/60/90.
GIVEN `the finding` IS A `What the commissioner is satisfied of`, `the disclosure` IS A `Disclosure`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax percentage under table 34 for` `the finding` `with` `the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the finding` EQUALS `concealment after being told of an investigation (TAA s 34)`
    THEN 90
    ELSE CONSIDER `the disclosure`
         WHEN `no disclosure` THEN `the basic penalty tax percentage for` `the finding`
         WHEN `disclosure in writing before being told of an investigation (TAA s 32)` THEN
             (`the basic penalty tax percentage for` `the finding` TIMES 20) DIVIDED BY 100
         WHEN `disclosure in writing after being told of an investigation, before it began (TAA s 33)` THEN
             (`the basic penalty tax percentage for` `the finding` TIMES 80) DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `the land tax payable` IS A NUMBER, `the finding` IS A `What the commissioner is satisfied of`, `the disclosure` IS A `Disclosure`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax under s 19A(4) on` `the land tax payable` `for` `the finding` `with` `the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the amount` LESS THAN 20 THEN 0 ELSE `to the nearest cent` `the amount`
    WHERE
        `the amount` MEANS (`the land tax payable` TIMES `the penalty tax percentage under table 34 for` `the finding` `with` `the disclosure`) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `s 17 -- payment`

-- s 17(1): "Land tax in relation to a parcel of land is payable to the commissioner by the owner of the parcel." (2): the
-- owner is liable for unpaid land tax "whether the amount became payable before or after the person became the owner".
-- (4): "The assessment notice for the land tax payable for a quarter ... must state a date for payment of the land tax
-- (the payment date). (5) The payment date must not be earlier than 4 weeks after the date of the notice." (6): the
-- owner may pay "(a) ... on or before the date for the payment ..., the amount of the land tax; or (b) by paying the
-- amounts on the days that the person wishes, but so that the amount owing on the date for payment is paid no later
-- than the date for payment." Clock: days from the date of the notice. LEST: s 19 interest for each month or part of a
-- month (TAA s 25 does not apply, s 19(3)).
GIVEN `the payment date` IS A DATE, `the notice date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment date` `is a lawful land tax payment date for a notice dated` `the notice date` IF
    (`the day that is` 28 `days after` `the notice date`) `is on or before` `the payment date`

GIVEN `days to the payment date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
DECIDE `s 17 -- the owner must pay the land tax by the payment date` IS
    PARTY `the owner`
    MUST  `pay the land tax`
    WITHIN `days to the payment date`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "Land Tax Act s 17: the land tax was not paid by the payment date; s 19: interest for each month or part of a month it remains unpaid (TAA s 25 does not apply, s 19(3))"

§§ `s 11D(3) -- extending the exemption after a death`

-- s 11D(3): "Before the 2-year period ends, the personal representative may apply, in writing, to the commissioner to
-- extend the period. (4) The application must set out the grounds on which it is made." s 11E(1): "On receiving an
-- application under section 11D, the commissioner may extend the period". s 11E(3): the commissioner "must tell the
-- personal representative, in writing, of the decision". s 11F: the commissioner may allow a later application. Clock:
-- days from the owner's death. The period ends at the end of its last day (above, with s 11D(2)), so an application on
-- that day is made before it ends: WITHIN counts the last day in.
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from the death to the last day to apply under s 11D(3), for a death on` `the day of the death` MEANS
    `the number of days from` `the day of the death` `to` (`the last day of the 2-year period after a death on` `the day of the death`)

GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
DECIDE `s 11D(3) -- the personal representative may apply before the 2 years end to extend the exemption` IS
    PARTY `the personal representative`
    DO    `apply in writing to extend the 2-year period`
    WITHIN `the days from the death to the last day to apply under s 11D(3), for a death on` `the day of the death`
    HENCE
        (PARTY `the commissioner`
         MUST  `decide whether to extend the period`)
    LEST  FULFILLED
